B.8 Sign Convention for the Normal Compression

The normal compression at contact ij is defined from the geometric distance between the deformed surfaces. Let \mathbf{X}_I^{ij} and \mathbf{X}_{II}^{ij} be the material points on the ball and raceway that lie on the common normal, and let \mathbf{u}_I^{ij} and \mathbf{u}_{II}^{ij} be their displacements. Let \mathbf{n}^{ij} be the outward unit normal at the raceway contact point, oriented from body I toward body II.

The signed distance between the surfaces, measured along \mathbf{n}^{ij}, is:

g_{ij}(\mathbf{q}, \mathbf{x}_c) = g_{0,ij} + (\mathbf{u}_{II}^{ij} - \mathbf{u}_I^{ij})^\top \mathbf{n}^{ij},
\tag{B.27}

where g_{0,ij} is the initial gap (positive if separated, negative if preloaded interference). The normal compression is:

\delta_{ij} = -g_{ij} = -g_{0,ij} - (\mathbf{u}_{II}^{ij} - \mathbf{u}_I^{ij})^\top \mathbf{n}^{ij}.
\tag{B.28}

The kinematic relation in the thesis is written as:

\delta_{ij} = \delta_{0,ij} + \mathbf{n}_{ij}^\top \mathbf{B}_{ij}\mathbf{q} - \mathbf{g}_{ij}^\top \mathbf{x}_c - \Delta g_{ij}(\mathbf{u}_{\text{ring}}),
\tag{B.29}

where \delta_{0,ij} = -g_{0,ij}, \mathbf{n}_{ij}^\top\mathbf{B}_{ij}\mathbf{q} aggregates the deformations of the crown, ring, and ball along the normal, and \Delta g_{ij} is the additional gap change due to ring deformation. The sign convention is: an increase in \delta_{ij} is an increase in compression, and corresponds to an increase in Q_{ij}.

The function \Delta g_{ij}(\mathbf{u}_{\text{ring}}) can be positive or negative depending on the local geometry; it is not assigned a sign by convention. The implementation must compute it from the deformed normal and verify at each iteration that g_{ij} and Q_{ij} are non-negative and complementary.

